course: dictionary
lesson: 14878
title: Recapture: taking back and bringing back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Recapture means to catch or take something again. The start of the word, re-, means again, and capture means to catch or take. So recapture means capture again.
explain: «The zookeepers recaptured the lion after it escaped.» The lion had got out before, so recaptured means the keepers caught it again.
explain: «The army recaptured the town from the enemy.» Here recaptured means taking back a place. The word can also bring back a feeling: «The film recaptures the magic of childhood» means the film brings that magic back.
fact: Recapture means to catch or take back something that was lost or taken.
fact: «Recapture» can mean catching an escaped animal or prisoner again.
fact: «Recapture» can mean taking back a town or fort from an enemy.
fact: «Recapture» can also mean bringing back a feeling, a memory or a mood.
fact: As a noun, a recapture is the act of catching or taking something again.
exercise: «The police recaptured the escaped prisoner two days later.» What does recaptured mean? | *Caught again | Hid from | Let go free | Thanked
exercise: «The film recaptures the magic of childhood.» What does recaptures mean here? | Makes a film about trains | Throws away | *Brings back a feeling | Sells old tickets
exercise: The re- at the start of recapture means what? | Under | *Again | Very | Not
test: «The army hoped to recapture the fort before winter.» What does recapture mean here? | To fall asleep | *To take back a place from the enemy | To sing a song | To build a new fort from scratch
test: «Can the band recapture the sound of their first album?» What does recapture mean? | To delete the album | *To bring back a sound they had before | To buy a new guitar | To play the song slower
exam: Which sentence uses recapture as a noun, meaning the act of catching again? | The keepers will recapture the lion tomorrow. | *The quick recapture of the lion made everyone cheer. | The lion recaptured its freedom. | They ran to recapture the ball.
